\pard\lang2057\fs20 \b\fs24 SAMSUNG TV (WebSocket) - Unofficial Control4 driver\b0\fs20\par\par
\par\b DESCRIPTION\b0\par
Controls Samsung Tizen Smart TVs (2016 and later, K/M/N/Q/T/A/B/C series) through the TV's local APIs. The protocol is not official: it was reverse-engineered by the community (samsungtvws, Home Assistant). No cloud, no licensing, unencrypted Lua.\par
Three communication channels:\par
\li284\fi-284 - WebSocket (port chosen in the Port property): remote control, i.e. keys, navigation, transport.\par\pard\lang2057\fs20 
\li284\fi-284 - REST http, port 8001: ON/OFF state (PowerState) with adaptive polling, every 2 s while the TV is on and every 10 s while it is off.\par\pard\lang2057\fs20 
\li284\fi-284 - REST https, port 8002: application launch.\par\pard\lang2057\fs20 
\par\b REQUIREMENTS\b0\par
\li284\fi-284 - TV and Control4 controller on the same subnet/VLAN: TVs refuse WebSocket connections from other subnets.\par\pard\lang2057\fs20 
\li284\fi-284 - On the TV: Device Connection Manager > Access Notification = First Time Only.\par\pard\lang2057\fs20 
\li284\fi-284 - Static IP address or DHCP reservation for the TV.\par\pard\lang2057\fs20 
\li284\fi-284 - Tested on Control4 OS 3.4.3 with Composer Pro 3.4.3.\par\pard\lang2057\fs20 
\par\b SETUP\b0\par
\li284\fi-284 1. Add the driver in Composer Pro and set IP Address. Port: 8002 is recommended for 2018+ models; Device Name is the name the controller shows on the TV.\par\pard\lang2057\fs20 
\li284\fi-284 2. Set the Pairing property to "Pair with TV" and accept the popup that appears on the TV within 60 seconds.\par\pard\lang2057\fs20 
\li284\fi-284 3. Pairing Status becomes "Paired". Later connections are silent, with no popup.\par\pard\lang2057\fs20 
\li284\fi-284 4. For the Watch experience, bind the official Control4 minidrivers to the driver's MiniApp 1-9 slots.\par\pard\lang2057\fs20 
\par\b WATCH EXPERIENCE AND MINIAPPS\b0\par
The driver exposes the "Samsung App Switcher" proxy (avswitch) with 9 MiniApp slots, in this order: Netflix, YouTube, Prime Video, Disney+, Spotify, Apple TV, DAZN, RaiPlay, Paramount+. Binding minidrivers to the slots makes the tiles appear in the Navigator, and selecting one launches the app on the TV. If the TV is off, the driver waits for it to turn on (up to about 15 seconds) and then launches the app.\par
With an app open, the Navigator's on-screen keypad sends PASSTHROUGH commands (arrows, ENTER, MENU, PLAY, PAUSE...) translated into the matching Samsung keys. EJECT closes the app (KEY_EXIT).\par
\par\b COMMANDS\b0\par
\li284\fi-284 - ON/OFF aware of the real state: no unwanted toggle if the TV is already in the requested state.\par\pard\lang2057\fs20 
\li284\fi-284 - Volume and channels repeat while a button is held (stops on release or after 20 s).\par\pard\lang2057\fs20 
\li284\fi-284 - Mute, numbers, navigation, transport, colour keys, HDMI 1-3 input selection.\par\pard\lang2057\fs20 
\li284\fi-284 - Composer Programming: SEND_KEY (KeyCode parameter, e.g. KEY_HOME, KEY_HDMI1) and LAUNCH_APP (AppName parameter, e.g. Netflix).\par\pard\lang2057\fs20 
\li284\fi-284 - Keys that cannot be sent within 5 seconds (TV unreachable) are dropped: no "late" commands.\par\pard\lang2057\fs20 
\par\b EVENTS\b0\par
The driver notifies state changes to the TV proxy: the Power On and Power Off events are available in Programming. Power Off is confirmed by two consecutive readings, so it is detected within a few seconds and a single network glitch does not produce a false Power Off. When the driver restarts, the initial state is read without generating events.\par
\par\b LOGGING AND DIAGNOSIS\b0\par
Log Mode (Off, Print, Log, Print and Log; default Off) and Log Level (0 Alert ... 5 Debug; default 3 Info) set destination and detail. Every line has a tag: [REST] state, [WS] WebSocket, [PAIR] pairing, [CMD] commands, [APP] app launch, [LIFECYCLE] and [DRIVER] lifecycle and errors. The pairing token never appears in the logs. For a bug report set Log Mode = Print and Log Level = 5 - Debug.\par
\par\b TROUBLESHOOTING\b0\par
\li284\fi-284 - Popup on every connection: the token was not saved. Run Pairing = Unpair and then Pair with TV, accepting the popup.\par\pard\lang2057\fs20 
\li284\fi-284 - No popup while pairing: check that the TV is on and the IP is correct; check blocked devices in Device Connection Manager; try changing Device Name.\par\pard\lang2057\fs20 
\li284\fi-284 - Changed IP or Device Name: the token may no longer be valid; if commands stop working, pair again (a changed IP clears the token automatically).\par\pard\lang2057\fs20 
\li284\fi-284 - App launch times out: on 2022+ models the endpoint only answers over HTTPS on 8002; the driver handles this by itself.\par\pard\lang2057\fs20 
\li284\fi-284 - The WebSocket session closes by itself after about 20 seconds: this is normal firmware behaviour; the driver reconnects on the next command with no new popup.\par\pard\lang2057\fs20 
\par\b NOTES\b0\par
\li284\fi-284 - The TV never switches off completely: it stays in standby with the network active, so ON and OFF work from standby and Wake-on-LAN is not needed. If power to the TV is cut, it cannot be turned back on.\par\pard\lang2057\fs20 
\li284\fi-284 - The driver does not use the proprietary protocol of the official Samsung drivers for Control4 (port 1515, IR).\par\pard\lang2057\fs20 
Unofficial driver, provided "as is" without warranty, MIT licence. Samsung and Tizen are trademarks of their respective owners. Source code, full guide and issue tracker: https://github.com/DidyMond/Control4-Samsung-TV-WebSocket\par
